@@ -7,6 +7,35 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+* Added a CVE IDs field to library findings and report findings
+  * Findings store a validated list of CVE identifiers, which is copied when a finding is added to a report or a report finding is cloned to the library
+  * The collaborative finding forms have a CVE IDs editor that upper-cases entries and ignores anything that is not a CVE identifier
+  * The IDs are available to report templates as `finding.cves`, in the JSON and Excel reports, in finding CSV imports and exports as a `cves` column, and through the GraphQL API
+  * The findings library can be filtered and searched by CVE ID, shows the IDs on finding pages, and offers a hidden-by-default CVE IDs table column
+  * The new `extract_cves` management command fills the field from CVE identifiers already written in findings' text
+* Added a local copy of the CISA KEV catalog and FIRST EPSS scores, refreshed on a schedule you set
+  * Both sources are off by default; the new Vulnerability Intelligence Configuration page enables them and sets the update frequency (every 6 or 12 hours, daily, weekly, or manual) and the time of day
+  * Saving the configuration creates, changes, or removes the Django Q schedule for the refresh, and the page shows the next run, the last results, and a Refresh Now button
+  * The whole KEV catalog is kept, with removed entries marked; EPSS scores are kept for the CVE IDs findings reference, and a CVE ID newly added to a finding is looked up through FIRST's API
+  * Downloads are checked for size, shape, and age, so a failed or truncated download never replaces stored data
+  * The `import_kev` and `import_epss` management commands load offline copies, and `refresh_vuln_intel` runs a refresh from the command line
+  * The data is available read-only in the admin panel and through GraphQL (`knownExploitedVulnerability` and `epssScore`) for the user and manager roles
+* Added KEV and EPSS data for each finding's CVE IDs to reports and finding pages
+  * Report templates get `finding.kev`, `kev_cves`, `kev_due_date`, `kev_ransomware`, `epss_max`, `epss_max_percentile`, `epss_max_cve`, `epss_over_threshold`, and a per-CVE `vuln_intel` list, plus a report-level `vuln_intel` with the dates the data was current and three new `totals`; the template linter knows them all
+  * The Excel report adds KEV, KEV Due Date, Known Ransomware Use, Highest EPSS, and EPSS Percentile columns
+  * Library finding pages show a KEV badge and EPSS score for each CVE ID, and the findings library and report findings tables show one KEV badge and the highest EPSS score per finding
+  * A new EPSS threshold setting (10% by default) highlights high scores and sets `totals.findings_epss_over`
+  * Every KEV and EPSS date also comes in `YYYY-MM-DD` form, in a key ending in `_iso` (such as `finding.kev_due_date_iso`), so templates can compare dates whatever the server's date format
+
+### Fixed
+
+* Fixed the severity under each finding in the default Word template being blank; the template now prints `severity_rt` with the `{{r ... }}` rich-text tag
+* Fixed the default report and project download filenames omitting the project type; they referred to `project.project_type`, which is not in the report context, and now use `project.type` (a migration updates saved filenames that use the old variable)
+* Fixed template footnote styles never being applied when a Word template names them `footnote text` and `footnote reference`, and report generation failing when a template names the paragraph style `Footnote Text`; the template linter now also describes Footnote Text as a paragraph style
+* Fixed PowerPoint finding notes starting with the literal text `finding["title"]` instead of the finding's title, and a stray comma under the network detection heading
+
